+# GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c (CVE-2025-55184) — False Positive / Already Addressed for next@14.2.29
+
+## Summary
+
+**GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c does not require a separate security patch on next@14.2.29.**
+The vulnerability is the original React Server Components cyclic-thenable DoS
+(CVE-2025-55184). The incomplete-fix follow-up **GHSA-5j59-xgg2-r9c4
+(CVE-2025-67779)** ships the complete cycle-protection counter (`cycleProtection > 1000`)
+in `Chunk.prototype.then`. That follow-up patch fully covers this advisory.
+
+## Advisory
+
+- **GHSA:** GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c
+- **CVE:** CVE-2025-55184
+- **Package:** next@14.2.29
+- **Description:** Crafted HTTP requests to App Router Server Function endpoints can
+  cause the RSC deserializer to hang / consume CPU (cyclic thenables).
+- **Upstream affected range:** `>= 13.3.0, < 14.2.34` (and later 15.x/16.x lines)
+- **Upstream patched versions:** 14.2.34, 15.0.6, …
+- **Follow-up advisory:** GHSA-5j59-xgg2-r9c4 / CVE-2025-67779 (incomplete-fix follow-up)
+
+## Why this version is covered without a second patch
+
+next@14.2.29 is in the affected range. The same vendored
+`dist/compiled/react-server-dom-*` `Chunk.prototype.then` INITIALIZED path is
+hardened by the GHSA-5j59-xgg2-r9c4 patch applied to this package version.
+Applying the original (incomplete) CVE-2025-55184 change as a second patch would
+conflict with that follow-up on the same hunks.
+
+## References
+
+- https://github.com/vercel/next.js/security/advisories/GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c
+- https://github.com/vercel/next.js/security/advisories/GHSA-5j59-xgg2-r9c4
+- https://nextjs.org/blog/security-update-2025-12-11
+- https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-55184

